      m_Calls: []
  m_text: After receiving a teammate header at feet (open play or corner) or recovering
    an opponent's ball, a goalkeeper may run with it. At the successful end of the
    entire <link="movement_phase"><color=#79CEF2><u>Movement Phase</u></color></link>,
    if the keeper still holds possession inside their own penalty area, choose [H]
    pickup without another catch roll or [F] continue at feet. Pickup offers Quick
    Throw [Q] without Final Thirds, or normal goalkeeper distribution [K] through
    the Save and Hold Final Thirds sequence. Feet retains Movement, Standard Pass,
    High Pass and Long Ball options; eligibility persists through subsequent Movement
    Phases until pickup or passing. No mid-phase pickup is offered, including when
    collecting a nearby header. Teammate kicked Ground Passes, First Time Passes,
    High Passes and Long Balls always go to feet and never grant handling permission.
    A deliberate Drop Ball forbids picking up again; location alone never grants
    handling permission.
