      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Receiving a header at feet avoids the immediate catch risk and grants eligibility
    for the pickup choice after a completed Movement Phase inside the keeper's own
    penalty area. This applies to open play and corners, including nearby headers
    collected during movement. Outside-box receptions remain at feet; the keeper
    may use their remaining movement allowance to return inside. Choosing feet preserves
    eligibility through later Movement Phases while that keeper retains possession,
    until pickup or passing.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c5fdfdb697f0641feb89600dc51bf367, type: 2}
